1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,101
This tutorial shows a Tenant's own view of
rent

2
00:00:03,101 --> 00:00:06,202
in Oasis Crest Properties, signed in as
Ahmed Hassan.

3
00:00:06,202 --> 00:00:09,648
The home page shows the next payment:
21,250, due on

4
00:00:09,648 --> 00:00:13,094
the first of October and still within the
grace period.

5
00:00:13,094 --> 00:00:14,472
Select View all payments.

6
00:00:14,472 --> 00:00:17,229
My Payments opens with what is due now.

7
00:00:17,229 --> 00:00:19,641
The amount due is 21,250: cheque 5,

8
00:00:19,641 --> 00:00:22,053
number 200104, dated the first of October.

9
00:00:22,053 --> 00:00:25,498
The landlord already holds this cheque and
banks it on

10
00:00:25,498 --> 00:00:28,599
its date, so keep the funds in your
account.

11
00:00:28,599 --> 00:00:31,356
Its row shows the due date, the amount

12
00:00:31,356 --> 00:00:34,113
payable and the running total of
everything due.

13
00:00:34,113 --> 00:00:36,180
Payment History reads the other way.

14
00:00:36,180 --> 00:00:38,937
Cheques 1, 2 and 3 have cleared, and

15
00:00:38,937 --> 00:00:41,349
each has a receipt voucher to download.

16
00:00:41,349 --> 00:00:43,761
Cheque 4 is at the bank, awaiting

17
00:00:43,761 --> 00:00:46,173
clearance, so there is nothing to pay.

18
00:00:46,173 --> 00:00:49,963
Select Receipt Voucher on any cleared
cheque to download its receipt.

19
00:00:49,963 --> 00:00:54,098
From these two pages a Tenant can see what
is due, what

20
00:00:54,098 --> 00:00:57,888
has already moved, and the proof of what
has been paid.
